# Hardware and RFID Safety

- Do not modify the verified Zebra CUSTOM JSON in
  `gmdc_common/gmdc_common/services/rfid_control.py` without explicit approval.
  The fixed contract uses antennas 5/6, TID pointer 6, length 24, mask
  `800600`, 31/31 power, and per-antenna reporting.
- Keep FC1/FC2 reads and FC5/FC6 writes strict; never cross-fallback.
- A failed sensor read must not become a stale or invented sensor value.
- I/O health loss must remain a workflow safety lock.
- Distinguish a Modbus exception response from a transport/socket failure.
  Preserve the current soft-failure debounce and fresh-read reconnect behavior.
- Test failed writes and failed reads explicitly; a failed output must not claim
  that the physical device changed state.
